  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1240 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nLong range models are still honing in on the details of our next\nimpactful upper level system. A deepening trough in the northern\nPacific will eventually transitions south into the western CONUS.\nBefore then, a weak cutoff low will move into the Plains and aid\nin moisture advection and create positive vorticity in our CWA for\nthe start of the new workweek. Since this first system is weaker \nand further west than previous model runs, PoPs Tuesday and \nWednesday are decreasing in the Panhandles and are more focused on\nthe states to our west. The main system is now not expected to \nimpact the High Plains until later in the week and into next \nweekend. The current NBM and LREF ensemble members show increasing\nrain chances Thursday onward, but there are still a lot of \nuncertainties regarding QPF. The latest ensemble guidance has \nhigher chances for 24 hour QPF less than 0.1\" and much lower \nchances for 24 hour QPF greater than 0.5\" for the late week. Of \ncourse, with the highest impacts from this system more likely 7 \ndays out, there still time for the details to become more resolved\nconcerning this system's potential.\n\nRangel",
